# The kit's Verus files, one a line: the files `make verus-headers`
# (headers.sh) holds a port's copies of, each to the template of the same
# name in the package's templates/ (/usr/share/proved-port/templates/).
# Each is held by its header, its leading `#` comment (in a port's copy,
# ending before a `# kit:` line the copy still has), but
# .chainguard/review-prompt.md, which is held by its kit rule (the
# `- The kit` item). The kit's other templates (conformance, consumers,
# fuzz, test, lint, the environments, develop.yaml, deps.yaml) are
# starting points the port reshapes, and are not held.
